# Celar Protocol — build & local state
# (repo-wide ignores also live in ../.gitignore)

# Go build artifacts (chain/celard)
*.exe
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt
profile.out

# Local node / devnet home data — never commit chain state
.evmd/
.celard/
.testnets/
**/node[0-9]*/
data/
*.db

# Validator & node secrets — MUST never be committed
priv_validator_key.json
priv_validator_state.json
node_key.json
*.mnemonic
*.seed

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
._*
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Rust build artifacts
target/

# Python virtualenv for the FHE harness
.venv/
.runlog/

# KMS ceremony run outputs & TLS material — MUST never be committed
# (ceremony/ holds unprotected party shares from dev runs; certs/ holds
# private keys. See kms/celar-kms/ceremony/DEV-KEYS-WARNING.txt)
kms/celar-kms/ceremony*/
kms/celar-kms/certs/
kms/celar-kms/epoch*/
dkg-out/
epoch-out/
# Dev roster generated by `celar-kms-node roster-init`: it pins the digests of
# the local (ignored) dev CAs, so it is meaningless outside this machine. A
# real roster is authored during vetting and belongs in the deployment repo.
kms/celar-kms/roster.json
*.share.bin
key_*.pem

# Local working copy of a doc-repo file; canonical version lives in
# doc/engg/celar-onboarding-track-b.md
/celar-onboarding-track-b.md
